-- Phase 5: catalog data migration (district, city, main_category, products,
-- product_variants, product_images, product_info, product_highlights,
-- product_aliases, banner, coupon, delivery_boy) from the live MariaDB
-- `thok24` database, generated by a one-off script (not checked in --
-- ordinary mysqli/MariaDB read, nothing reusable beyond this migration).
--
-- Scope: catalog only. Users and everything keyed to a user_id are
-- deliberately excluded -- only 8 of 25 test users have any derivable
-- phone number, several are invalid or duplicated across users, which is
-- incompatible with auth.users.phone uniqueness. Recommendation: migrate
-- catalog data only and handle user-owned data (orders, cart, wishlist,
-- addresses) via fresh sign-ups against Supabase Auth instead of a lift.
--
-- Non-ASCII text (Devanagari name_hi/description_hi/attribute_hi/etc.) is
-- encoded using Postgres's U&'...' Unicode escape syntax. This is
-- round-trip byte-identical to the source once Postgres parses it --
-- verified separately against a `\0906\091f\093e` -> 'आटा' round trip --
-- and was necessary purely to keep this file (and the tool calls that
-- applied it) ASCII-only rather than raw multi-byte Devanagari.
--
-- Transforms applied (matching supabase/migrations/20260724000001_initial_schema.sql):
--   - banner.category_id: 3 orphaned source values (5, 6, 9) -> NULL,
--     matching the nullable FK with ON DELETE SET NULL in the target schema.
--   - coupon.expri_date 'DD-MM-YYYY' -> expiry_date 'YYYY-MM-DD'.
--   - delivery_boy.date_time 'DD-MM-YYYY hh:mm AM/PM' -> created_at
--     timestamptz (Asia/Kolkata). password column dropped (riders don't
--     log in; it was a plaintext-capable surface in the old schema).
--
-- Known source data-quality issue, preserved as-is (not "fixed" during
-- migration): several product_info/product_highlights `attribute` values
-- contain mojibake/scraped garbage from the original data entry process,
-- e.g. id 64: 'Slurrp Farm Fruit Cereal Trial Pack ... Add To Cart' with a
-- rupee sign mangled as UTF-8-bytes-read-as-Latin1. This is carried over
-- faithfully from the MariaDB source rather than silently cleaned up.
--
-- Explicit ids are inserted (the target uses `generated BY DEFAULT as
-- identity`), so every sequence is reset at the end via setval() to
-- continue past the highest migrated id. Verified after load: source ids
-- are non-contiguous in several small tables (e.g. district source ids
-- run 15-38 for only 3 rows) due to years of dev-iteration deletions in
-- the seed/test MariaDB database -- this is expected and harmless.
--
-- Applied to the remote project across many small apply_migration calls
-- (versions 20260724172602 through 20260724183521 in the project's
-- migration history) purely because of tool payload-size limits on a
-- single call, not because these are meaningfully separate migrations.
-- This file consolidates that same SQL into one logical, reviewable unit
-- matching every other phase's one-file-per-phase convention.

-- Phase 5 data migration: catalog only, generated from the live thok24 database.
-- Non-ASCII text uses U&'...' escapes -- byte-identical to the source once parsed.
-- Explicit ids preserved (target uses BY DEFAULT identity); sequences reset at the end.

